# Set by the QUIT / exit-program / shutdown handlers just before they call
# sys.exit(), so long-lived background daemon threads (media pre-cache
# probing, etc.) can notice we're closing and stop themselves on their own
# terms instead of racing the interpreter's teardown and getting caught
# mid-ThreadPoolExecutor-submit when it starts shutting down.
_app_shutting_down = threading.Event()

# Serializes _deferred_metadata_probing_worker runs. A file-add event spawns
# one of these per batch with no cap, so back-to-back adds (or one big
# folder import) used to leave 2-3 of them alive at once, each freely
# shelling out to ffprobe/ffmpeg via get_media_duration()/loudness probing
# with no regard for whether a video was actively playing -- confirmed in
# app_log.txt as the concurrent _deferred_metadata_probing_worker +
# _probe_and_patch_durations + _readerthread pile-up behind the worst
# FRAME GAP spikes (980ms/1417ms/1337ms), all on plain TV channels with
# nothing else unusual going on. Acquiring this before doing any real work
# means a second/third batch just waits its turn instead of piling on
# concurrently; each worker still finishes its own batch fully before the
# next one starts, same as before, just not several at once.
_deferred_metadata_probe_lock = threading.Lock()

